description:
Design a 2-bit binary counter with reset functionality. The counter increments its value on the rising edge of the clock signal (CLK) and wraps around to zero when it reaches the maximum value (3 in binary: 2'b11). It can be asynchronously reset to zero when the active low reset signal (RESET_B) is asserted, ensuring that the counter starts from a known state.
module top_module(
    Q      ,
    CLK    ,
    RESET_B
);

code:
module top_module(
    Q      ,
    CLK    ,
    RESET_B
);// Module ports
    output reg [1:0] Q      ;
    input  CLK            ;
    input  RESET_B        ;

    // Local signals
    reg [1:0] next_Q;

    // Counter logic
    always @(posedge CLK, negedge RESET_B) begin
        if (~RESET_B) begin
            Q <= 2'b00;
        end else begin
            next_Q <= Q + 1;
            if (next_Q == 2'b11) begin
                Q <= 2'b00;
            end else begin
                Q <= next_Q;
            end
        end
    end

endmodule

