description:
Develop a circuit that manages an asynchronous reset functionality with a counter. When the reset signal is low, the counter resets to zero and sets the output `rst` to high, indicating an active reset state. Upon the rising edge of the clock, if the reset is not active, the counter increments until it reaches a value of 10, at which point the output `rst` is set low, deactivating the reset condition. This module effectively generates a controlled reset signal that can be released after a set delay, defined by the counter.
module top_module(
  input reset,
  input clk,
  output rst
);

code:
module top_module(
  input reset,
  input clk,
  output rst
);reg [3:0] counter;
  reg rst_active;

  always @(posedge clk or negedge reset) begin
    if (!reset) begin
      counter <= 0;
      rst_active <= 1'b1;
    end else begin
      if (counter == 4'd10) begin
        rst_active <= 1'b0;
      end else begin
        counter <= counter + 1;
      end
    end
  end

  assign rst = rst_active;

endmodule

